{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1492326-using-saints-and-monsters-to-homebrew-abrahamic-religions-into-the-game","id":1492326,"title":"Using Saints and Monsters to homebrew Abrahamic religions into the game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-04T18:04:11-07:00","id":1492326,"title":"Using Saints and Monsters to homebrew Abrahamic religions into the game?","content":"So, there have always been two big things that kept these religions out of the in game spotlight. The first being that it could easily make a bunch of people mad about them being used in a game and the second being that these religions just don't really do the whole 'divine beings frequently come down and bone humans to make awesome super powered hybrid beings' thing. It happened once in Christianity and it is treated as a super special one time deal God will never do again while I don't think it ever happens at all in Judaism or Islam. But you know what those religions have a ton of? Prophets and miracle workers who can easily be fluffed as Saints, Prophets, and patronage Sorcerers powered by the Abrahamic God. So if you wanted to have an answer to 'why do people follow these religions when they don't play ball with the miracle slinging scions like the other deities' you could give those religions a higher then average number of Saints, Prophets, and Sorcerers then the other kinds produce to 'balance out' the fact that they have no scions running around representing them. That way they do have people running around doing awesome magical miracles to defend members of those faiths and make them an attractive option in the war for believers the various religions fight against each other in setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I'm not sure how well it would work, but you could even maybe mollify people who are mad about you including it in the game and therefore declaring a 'correct' version of God. Saints draw power from being true to their cultural/religious virtues, you could have both a baptist saint and a catholic saint and not need to declare either of them right because all that matters is that the saint <i>believes </i>themselves to be right. And who is to say if a prophet who insists they are a messenger of Allah is really that or if they just went a bit crazy after seeing the tapestry of fate broke their mind and they only <i>think </i>it is true? And maybe that 'miracle worker' patronage sorcerer televangelist on TV doing faith healings on live tv made a pact with Jesus, or maybe they are a grifting charlatan who made a pact with some other supernatural being but saw a way to make a quick buck by <i>pretending </i>their patron is Jesus. Though again, I'm not sure how well these things would work for defusing someone that is mad at you for including their religion alongside a bunch of other 'fake pagan nonsense' in a role playing game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, thoughts on if the introduction of Saints, Prophets, and Sorcerers as playable might be a good way to homebrew in an explanation how they could be competitive in setting despite lacking miracle slinging scions to help draw in believers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 09-04-2022, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T04:48:49-07:00","id":1492358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1492326-using-saints-and-monsters-to-homebrew-abrahamic-religions-into-the-game#post1492326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there have always been two big things that kept these religions out of the in game spotlight. The first being that it could easily make a bunch of people mad about them being used in a game and the second being that these religions just don't really do the whole 'divine beings frequently come down and bone humans to make awesome super powered hybrid beings' thing. It happened once in Christianity and it is treated as a super special one time deal God will never do again while I don't think it ever happens at all in Judaism or Islam. But you know what those religions have a ton of? Prophets and miracle workers who can easily be fluffed as Saints, Prophets, and patronage Sorcerers powered by the Abrahamic God. So if you wanted to have an answer to 'why do people follow these religions when they don't play ball with the miracle slinging scions like the other deities' you could give those religions a higher then average number of Saints, Prophets, and Sorcerers then the other kinds produce to 'balance out' the fact that they have no scions running around representing them. That way they do have people running around doing awesome magical miracles to defend members of those faiths and make them an attractive option in the war for believers the various religions fight against each other in setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I'm not sure how well it would work, but you could even maybe mollify people who are mad about you including it in the game and therefore declaring a 'correct' version of God. Saints draw power from being true to their cultural/religious virtues, you could have both a baptist saint and a catholic saint and not need to declare either of them right because all that matters is that the saint <i>believes </i>themselves to be right. And who is to say if a prophet who insists they are a messenger of Allah is really that or if they just went a bit crazy after seeing the tapestry of fate broke their mind and they only <i>think </i>it is true? And maybe that 'miracle worker' patronage sorcerer televangelist on TV doing faith healings on live tv made a pact with Jesus, or maybe they are a grifting charlatan who made a pact with some other supernatural being but saw a way to make a quick buck by <i>pretending </i>their patron is Jesus. Though again, I'm not sure how well these things would work for defusing someone that is mad at you for including their religion alongside a bunch of other 'fake pagan nonsense' in a role playing game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, thoughts on if the introduction of Saints, Prophets, and Sorcerers as playable might be a good way to homebrew in an explanation how they could be competitive in setting despite lacking miracle slinging scions to help draw in believers?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T07:59:14-07:00","id":1492365,"title":"","content":"Yeah my Tzva\u2019ot project is focused on playing Saints and Prophets with Angelic Guides (though playable Nephilim are included too as mechanically Titan-Scions too)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T09:13:56-07:00","id":1492370,"title":"","content":"It's one of the reasons I've been interested in Saints and Monsters. My observations after reading it:<br /> <br /> 1. Saints are presented as Culture Heroes who embody the Virtues of the Pantheon, but don't necessarily worship any of the gods of the Pantheon. That doesn't mesh with Abrahamic Saints, but it's easy enough to fluff.<br /> <br /> 2. Prophets, on the other hand, work quite well in this regard; particularly the Miracleworkers.<br /> <br /> 3. Denizens can be used to model angels; in particular, the traditional view of angels fits under Winged remarkably well. Sadly, the book doesn't go into any detail about Denizens who have Legend by virtue of what they are, as opposed to who patronizes them. The section also doesn't have anything about nonhuman Denizens who would match notions of angels that <i>aren't</i> winged humanoids. Nevertheless, Denizens is the right overall approach for handling angels. Mostly. (See below.) Most Angels would likely operate at the Demigod level, though the most powerful of them would reach God tier in all but name, forming something not unlike a Pantheon. Again, more on this below.<br /> <br /> 4. Sorcerers are, in Christianity at least, rare. Jewish beliefs include a Kaballah Motif; and supposedly King Solomon was a practitioner. You <i>might</i> also create a Motif for Catholic Priests; and I don't know enough about Islam to know if it has anything suitable. By far, the most common Source of Power would be Patronage, by the One True God (or, more rarely, by an angel). That said, the most common Spells and Rituals seen in literature for Abrahamic Sorcerers seem to cut across the Workings, including things like Spirit-Wrestling, Ecstatic Trance, Sudden Insight, and Spirit Teacher.<br /> <br /> 5. Traditionally, the closest that Abrahamic faiths get to Titans are demons. If you allow angels to have scions, and you go with the idea that demons are fallen angels (not necessarily a given), then you could end up with demonic scions as well.<br /> <hr /><br /> But in addition to Saints and Monsters, I'd also consider looking at Masks of the Mythos and Dragon for inspiration; though applying these books to Abrahamic faiths would require <i>heavy</i> reimagining, largely keeping only Awareness and Inheritance. The key here is that Abrahamic religion doesn't necessarily mesh well with the concept of Legend; and the conceptual bases of Awareness or Inheritance might make for a better \u201cpower stat\u201d for followers of these religions.<br /> <br /> For Masks of the Mythos, if you scrape away the Eldritch Horrors aspect of the game, the mechanics of Awareness can be reskinned to represent humans who have encountered the Divine and been changed by it. Of particular interest is that Awareness <i>doesn't</i> take the character down the Hero/Demigod/God path; if you <i>just</i> have Awareness, you're basically \u201cstuck\u201d at Hero. Which fits most models of \u201choly men\u201d, which generally <i>don't</i> include them turning into Divine beings themselves. As well, while the motive for it is different, it's pointed out that the Mythos generally produces Chosen scions almost exclusively. Likewise, while Born Scions of the Abrahamic God are rare in the extreme (possibly numbering only one, if even that), Chosen Scions could potentially be far more common; especially in a setting where Scions of the Pantheons are so prominent.<br /> <br /> Dragon, meanwhile, could probably be reskinned as a game system for handling angels. More generally, my complaint about the lack of material about Denizens that are designed to operate on the equivalent of Demigod or God levels can potentially be addressed by using Dragon as a template for how to do exactly that. Inheritance replaces Legend, in this case, and the Heir to an angelic Inheritance, never quite human to begin with, becomes ever more angel-like as his Inheritance grows \u2014 as opposed to the Heir to a Dragon becoming more draconic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-15-2023, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T09:14:00-07:00","id":1492371,"title":"","content":"Seems great ! It works best for Saints and Prophets i think, regarding the attitude of those religions towards sorcery, but still, the book introduce, in the passage describing Necromancy, the witch of Endor, a biblical figure. And since Aten as infiltrated the Evangelical movement with the Clear Light Church, you can totally imagine a sorcerer posing as a miracle workers.<br /> <br /> As for the competitive aspect, a Saint can basically nullify the power of a Scion, and even a God. They are mechanically rigid, but really overpowered. This could totally explain how people attracted to their Virtues would join their faith and believe in them. It would also put the catholic and orthodox worship of relics in a all new light. I really dig the idea, as it allows us to better imagine the history of the World, how it can be close to ours, while radically different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sorry i am french ;__;","edited":{"userid":27418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","user":"Lady Darcia","date":". 09-06-2022, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","name":"Lady Darcia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T10:27:40-07:00","id":1492374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems great ! It works best for Saints and Prophets i think, regarding the attitude of those religions regarding sorcery, but still, the b